         MACRO
         XAIOBWRK
.*-----------------------------------------------------------------*
.*  XAIOB -- THE REENTRANT COUNTERPART OF XAIO.                     *
.*                                                                  *
.*  XAIO KEEPS ITS WORK AREAS IN A STATIC BLOCK AND FINDS A         *
.*  SUBCHANNEL BY SCANNING WITH STSCH.  BOTH CHOICES ARE RIGHT FOR  *
.*  THE MODULE IT WAS BUILT FOR AND WRONG HERE:                     *
.*                                                                  *
.*    A STATIC WORK AREA CANNOT BE USED BY A REENTRANT MODULE, AND  *
.*    DMKIOS, DMKIOT AND DMKCNS ALL DECLARE REENTRANT IN THEIR OWN  *
.*    PROLOGUES.                                                    *
.*                                                                  *
.*    THE STSCH SCAN EXISTS BECAUSE DMKDMP RUNS AFTER AN ABEND, WHEN*
.*    CP'S CONTROL BLOCKS ARE EXACTLY WHAT CANNOT BE TRUSTED.  THESE*
.*    THREE RUN WITH THE SYSTEM HEALTHY AND WITH THE BLOCKS ALREADY *
.*    IN HAND, SO THE SCAN WOULD BE UP TO 256 STSCHS TO LEARN WHAT  *
.*    RDEVSSID ALREADY SAYS.                                          *
.*                                                                  *
.*  SO THIS SET TAKES ITS SUBCHANNEL FROM RDEVSSID AND ITS STORAGE  *
.*  FROM THE IOBLOK, WHICH MAKES IT REENTRANT BY CONSTRUCTION: EVERY*
.*  BYTE IT WRITES BELONGS TO THE I/O IT IS DRIVING.                *
.*                                                                  *
.*  IT THEREFORE REQUIRES, AND DOES NOT CHECK, THAT                 *
.*                                                                  *
.*        USING RDEVBLOK,R8                                         *
.*        USING IOBLOK,R10                                          *
.*        USING PSA,R0                                              *
.*                                                                  *
.*  ARE ALL IN FORCE, AND THAT R8'S RDEVBLOK IS THE DEVICE BEING    *
.*  OPERATED ON.  ALL THREE MODULES ESTABLISH R8 AND R10 IN THEIR   *
.*  PROLOGUES AND NEVER DROP THEM.  THE THIRD CONDITION IS THE ONE  *
.*  TO CHECK PER SITE: IN DMKCNS EVERY CALLER GETS ITS DEVICE FROM  *
.*  CALL DMKSCNRD, WHICH RETURNS R8'S OWN ADDRESS, AND IN DMKIOT    *
.*  FROM IOBRADD OR FROM THE INTERRUPTING DEVICE, WHOSE RDEVBLOK IS *
.*  WHAT R8 HOLDS IN THE INTERRUPT HANDLER.                         *
.*                                                                  *
.*  THE BODIES ARE DMKIOS'S IOSX* SHIMS, WHICH HAVE ASSEMBLED CLEAN *
.*  SINCE RUN44, COPIED RATHER THAN REWRITTEN.  DMKIOS KEEPS ITS OWN*
.*  COPY FOR NOW AND SHOULD MOVE TO THIS MACRO ONCE M1 PASSES, SO   *
.*  THAT THE CHANGE IS MADE AGAINST A WORKING BASELINE INSTEAD OF   *
.*  BEFORE ONE EXISTS.                                              *
.*-----------------------------------------------------------------*
         SPACE 1
XAIOBORB DS    0H             ORB TEMPLATE. EVERYTHING BUT THE
*                             CCW ADDRESS, WHICH THE CALLER SET IN
*                             THE CAW AND WHICH IS COPIED IN BELOW.
         DC    F'0'           INTERRUPTION PARAMETER
         DC    X'00'          KEY, S, C, M, Y, F, P -- ALL ZERO
         DC    AL1(ORBCCWFM)  CCW FORMAT: ORBCCWFM, NOT A LITERAL
         DC    X'80'          LPM -- LOGICAL PATH MASK, NOT ZERO
         DC    X'00'          RESERVED
         SPACE 1
.*  R14 AND R15 ARE THE ONLY REGISTERS THESE TOUCH BESIDES R1, AND
.*  THE CALL-SITE MACRO SAVES R14, R15, R0 AND R1 IN IOBXSAV -- WHICH
.*  LIVES IN THE IOBLOK, SO TWO CONCURRENT I/OS SAVE INTO DIFFERENT
.*  PLACES.  THE LM THAT RESTORES THEM DOES NOT DISTURB THE CONDITION
.*  CODE THE SUBROUTINE SET.
         SPACE 1
XAIOBSIO DS    0H             SSCH, WITH SIO'S CONDITION CODES
         MVC   IOBORB(12),XAIOBORB  BUILD THE ORB
*  THE INTERRUPTION PARAMETER CARRIES THE DEVICE ADDRESS. IT IS
*  THE ONLY FIELD AN ESA/390 I/O INTERRUPT RETURNS THAT CP CHOOSES,
*  AND THE TEMPLATE ABOVE LEAVES IT ZERO -- SO DMKIOT'S
*  CLC IOINTPRM+2(2),IOBRADD MATCHED NO DEVICE AT ALL AND EVERY
*  ASYNCHRONOUS COMPLETION WAS DROPPED. DASD HID IT: ITS STATUS IS
*  NORMALLY PENDING AT SSCH, SO CC1 TAKES THE SYNCHRONOUS TSCH PATH
*  AND NEVER NEEDS AN INTERRUPT. I-174, WALL 16.
         MVC   IOBOPARM+2(2),IOBRADD  INT PARM = DEVICE ADDRESS
         MVC   IOBOCCW,CAW    CCW ADDRESS THE CALLER SET
         L     R1,RDEVSSID    X'0001' || SUBCHANNEL NUMBER
         SSCH  IOBORB         START SUBCHANNEL
         BR    R14            SSCH AND SIO AGREE ON CC0/2/3, AND
*                             THEIR CC1 DIFFERS IN WORDING ONLY
         SPACE 1
XAIOBTIO DS    0H             TSCH, WITH TIO'S CONDITION CODES
         L     R1,RDEVSSID    X'0001' || SUBCHANNEL NUMBER
         TSCH  IOBIRB         TEST SUBCHANNEL
         BC    4,XAIOBTIF     CC1: NOTHING PENDING -- BUT SEE BELOW
         BC    3,XAIOBTIX     CC2 AND CC3 PASS THROUGH UNCHANGED
         MVI   CSW,X'00'      BUILD THE CSW THE CALLER EXPECTS
         MVC   CSW+1(3),IOBICCW+1  CCW ADDRESS
         MVC   CSW+4(4),IOBIDST    STATUS AND RESIDUAL COUNT
         LA    R15,1          TELL THE CALLER CSW STORED,
         LCR   R15,R15        WHICH IS CC1. LTR WOULD GIVE CC2.
         BR    R14
.*  SEE XAIO.MACRO: TSCH CC1 MEANS "NOT STATUS-PENDING", WHICH IS THE
.*  ANSWER BOTH FOR AN IDLE SUBCHANNEL AND FOR ONE STILL RUNNING.  CP'S
.*  POLLING LOOPS LEAVE ON CC0, SO CALLING A RUNNING SUBCHANNEL "FREE"
.*  LETS THEM OUT EARLY.  THE SCSW DISTINGUISHES THE TWO CASES.
.*  I-93.
XAIOBTIF DS    0H             CC1: NO STATUS -- IDLE OR STILL RUNNING ?
         TM    IOBIRB+2,X'7F' FUNCTION OR ACTIVITY CONTROL SET ?
         BNZ   XAIOBTIB       YES -- S/370 WOULD HAVE SAID BUSY
         TM    IOBIRB+3,X'E0' SUBCHANNEL, DEVICE OR SUSPENDED ?
         BNZ   XAIOBTIB       YES -- BUSY
         SR    R15,R15        TRULY IDLE: ZERO RESULT, SO CC0
         BR    R14
XAIOBTIB DS    0H             BUSY.  CC2.
         LA    R15,1          POSITIVE, AND LTR ON A POSITIVE VALUE
         LTR   R15,R15        SETS CC2
XAIOBTIX DS    0H
         BR    R14
         SPACE 1
XAIOBHIO DS    0H             HSCH REPLACES HIO AND HDV ALIKE.
*                             THE DISTINCTION WAS BETWEEN HALTING A
*                             CHANNEL AND HALTING A DEVICE, AND A
*                             SUBCHANNEL IS ALWAYS EXACTLY ONE DEVICE.
         L     R1,RDEVSSID    X'0001' || SUBCHANNEL NUMBER
         HSCH  0              HALT SUBCHANNEL
         BR    R14
         SPACE 1
XAIOBCIO DS    0H             CSCH FOR CLRIO. THE ONLY CLRIO IN THE
*                             NUCLEUS IS DMKCNS'S, AND CSCH SETS ONLY
*                             CC0 -- CLEARED -- OR CC3 -- NOT VALID,
*                             NOT ENABLED OR NOT THERE.  THOSE ARE
*                             EXACTLY THE TWO THE CALLER TESTS.
         L     R1,RDEVSSID    X'0001' || SUBCHANNEL NUMBER
         CSCH  0              CLEAR SUBCHANNEL
         BR    R14
         MEND
.*
         MACRO
&NAME    XABSIO
&NAME    STM   R14,R1,IOBXSAV
         BAL   R14,XAIOBSIO
         LM    R14,R1,IOBXSAV
         MEND
.*
         MACRO
&NAME    XABTIO
&NAME    STM   R14,R1,IOBXSAV
         BAL   R14,XAIOBTIO
         LM    R14,R1,IOBXSAV
         MEND
.*
         MACRO
&NAME    XABHIO
&NAME    STM   R14,R1,IOBXSAV
         BAL   R14,XAIOBHIO
         LM    R14,R1,IOBXSAV
         MEND
.*
         MACRO
&NAME    XABCIO
&NAME    STM   R14,R1,IOBXSAV
         BAL   R14,XAIOBCIO
         LM    R14,R1,IOBXSAV
         MEND
